ideas to test: auxiliary heads, target recomputation in training






// n, m, maxply, a, B, lambda, train minibatch, lr, test games, train_epochs, optimizer, weight_decay, seed - are to be added to config.json aproprietly

arena is n games // game slot maintains game instance
for each arena slot game history vector (length = max possible ply = 80 ) // abreviated as ghv
big buffer is m slots
model is either resnet or katago, cast to bf16

while true:

    // states must be encoded
    start timer "model"
    evaluate n games with model from both player perspectives (model batch = 2n)
    end timer "model"

    start timer "cpu"
    calculate improved policy in fp32:   pi' = softmax_a( (Q(a) + B*log pi(a)) / (a + B) ) // mask illegal before softmax
    calculate value estimate  in fp32:   V_t = sum_a( pi' * Q )

    store to ghv: board (bitpacking 20B), scores (2 * u8 = 2B), played move (2 * u8 = 2B), pi' (2 * 80 * bf16 / 8b = 320B), V_t (2 * fp32 / 8b = 8B)

    step n games sampling from pi'

    if after step game i is terminal:
        backward calculate G_t in fp32:  G_t = (1-lambda)V_t+1 + lambda*G_t+1, G_T-1 = R_T
        // do not store terminal state
        store to big buffer: board (bitpacking 20B), scores (2 * u8 = 2B), played move (2 * u8 = 2B), pi' (2 * 80 * bf16 = 320B), G_t (2 * bf16 = 4B)
        clear ghv for game i
        init fresh game instance in arena slot i

    if big buffer has less than n*max_ply free slots remaining:
        // throwing away the non termianl games is faster than playing them to completion
        record number of states in big buffer, and number of states dropped from all n ghvs
        reset arena to fresh games
        reset all ghv
        stop timer "cpu"
        start timer "training"
        train model on big buffer, the target for policy is pi', the target for q is only for the played action, at S_t, G_t.
            inside training, keep time per minibatch
            one epoch per self-play cycle, with every position used once
        clear big buffer
        print stats per minibatch time in miliseconds (forward, backward, optimizer), loss
        stop timer "training"

        start timer "strength_test"
        test strength against previous model:
            play test_games number of games in parralel untill completion
            game is symetrical so player 0 is old model, player 1 new model
            as some games terminate, we do not change batch size, just input zero tensors in place, to avoid model recompilation
            play by argmax over raw policy, not pi'
        stop timer strength_test

        print stats for whole training step: total model time, total cpu time, total training time, strength_test time, in seconds :2f, win draw loss games against old model
    else if not:
        stop timer "cpu"
        print stats for arena step, cpu time, model time, in miliseconds


def bitpacking:
    // whether that is 20 i8s or 2 words and one i32 - i don't care
    the board is held in 80 i8, but each can only hold 4 states, hence pack 4 squares into 8 bits, so full game in 20B



